@@ -114,6 +114,24 @@ response. Gym consequently commits an ordinary token-free `CallRecord` before
 the response is released to the agent. No local metadata ledger or rollout-end
 conversion is involved in the active path.
 
+### Debug echo of staged tokens
+
+Gym's model-call debug trace (`model_call_debug_trace` in the Gym global
+config, set under `env.nemo_gym`) records each call's text beside its token
+data. Because both backends strip token arrays from captured responses, Gym
+asks for an echo with `ng_debug_tokens: true`: a top-level request field for
+the vLLM worker and an `offload_params` key for MInf. After staging, the vLLM
+worker's `_finish_request_capture` and `TQMegatronTokenStager` return the
+staged call's `prompt_token_ids`, `generation_token_ids`, and
+`generation_log_probs` (plus an `error` string when the payload could not be
+read) under the response field `ng_debug_tokens`. MInf merges stager metadata
+into the HTTP response. Gym's model server reads and removes the field before
+the response reaches the agent. The echo never changes what is staged or
+committed, and a request without the flag gets no echo. With token capture
+disabled and the trace enabled, the NemoGym environment stamps each row's
+`_ng_rollout_id` from its group id, generation index, and group attempt, so
+every traced call still carries its rollout id.
+
 ![Token capture custody](../assets/token-capture-ledger-queue-data-flow.png)
 
